Here is a single, formal patent-style independent method claim/description written in standard patent prose:

***

**A method for maintaining the dimensional integrity of an internal passage during sintering of a 3D-printed metal component, the method comprising:**

providing a green body composed of a powdered metallic material suspended in a binder matrix, the green body defining an internal passage having a lower interface and an upper interface; 

disposing a support structure within the internal passage, wherein the support structure comprises:
*   a first release layer contacting the lower interface of the internal passage;
*   a sacrificial support core positioned adjacent to the first release layer, the sacrificial support core composed of a refractory material configured to substantially maintain structural rigidity at a sintering temperature of the powdered metallic material; and
*   a second release layer positioned between the sacrificial support core and the upper interface of the internal passage, wherein the first and second release layers are composed of a ceramic material formulated to prevent diffusion bonding between the sacrificial support core and the metallic material;

thermal processing the green body and the disposition of the support structure at the sintering temperature to consolidate the powdered metallic material into a densified metal component, wherein the sacrificial support core physically supports the upper interface to prevent sagging of the internal passage during consolidation; and

evacuating the sacrificial support core and the first and second release layers from the internal passage of the densified metal component.

**1.** A method of fabricating a metal part using bound powder extrusion, comprising:

extruding a metallic build material comprising a metal powder bound within a binder matrix to form a green part, the green part defining an internal passage bounded by an inner wall;

depositing a ceramic interface material to form a ceramic release interface continuously surrounding an internal support region within the internal passage, wherein the ceramic release interface is positioned directly between the inner wall of the internal passage and the internal support region;

extruding a support material within the internal support region to form an internal support structure, such that the internal support structure is isolated from the inner wall by the ceramic release interface;

thermally densifying the green part by heating the green part to a sintering temperature to coalesce the metal powder into a sintered metal part, wherein during thermal densification:
> (i) the ceramic release interface acts as a physical diffusion barrier preventing metallic fusion between the internal support structure and the inner wall, and 
> (ii) the internal support structure and the ceramic release interface collectively maintain structural support against the inner wall to prevent geometric distortion of the internal passage during isotropic volumetric shrinkage; and

separating the internal support structure from the internal passage of the sintered metal part along the ceramic release interface.
